# Why: a post's address is its folder name, so renaming a folder moves the post. Old addresses that were
# shared or indexed point here to the new one, permanently, so no link to the blog ever breaks.

# The first post's folder followed its new title, "Talked out loud, tidied by AI" (October 2026).
/thoughts/2026-10-23-converted-with-ai /thoughts/2026-10-23-talked-out-loud-tidied-by-ai 301
/thoughts/2026-10-23-converted-with-ai.html /thoughts/2026-10-23-talked-out-loud-tidied-by-ai 301
/thoughts/2026-10-23-converted-with-ai/* /thoughts/2026-10-23-talked-out-loud-tidied-by-ai/:splat 301

# "Themes" became "Topics" (October 2026): the usual word on a blog, and it no longer reads like the
# light and dark theme switch.
/themes /topics 301
/themes.html /topics 301
/themes/* /topics/:splat 301
